    },
    {
      "id": "aLJB",
      "code_hash": "72453258b02018ad4462905f3df26138",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"part-b-heating-and-cooling-of-ferrite-core\">Part B: Heating and Cooling of Ferrite Core</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We measure the induced secondary voltage <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(V_s||)</marimo-tex> as a function of temperature <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T||)</marimo-tex> to identify the Curie temperature (<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T_c||)</marimo-tex>) where the magnetic phase transition occurs.\nWe fit the temperature-time profile <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T(t)||)</marimo-tex> during cooling to Newton's law of cooling:</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\\frac{dT}{dt} = -k(T - T_{\\text{env}})||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">which has the solution:</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[T(t) = T_{\\text{env}} + (T_0 - T_{\\text{env}}) e^{-kt}||]</marimo-tex></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
